55,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A is stable, B depends on unreliable contractors, C is a safety risk without certification, and D is a logistical nightmare.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"D is the only one that solves the transport crisis, but A could work if we use community halls in those wards.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"A's session fees are grant-funded for a year. That's a risk. B and C use the endowment for capital, which is better.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,B is just a repeat of the failed digitisation project. A mirrors the successful evening groups from six years ago.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"C requires tool certification we don't have. A requires facilitators, but we can't supervise them. D is too much for staff.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, if A uses partner organizations, maybe the partners handle the supervision? That reduces our dependency.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If we put Language Circles in the outer wards, we solve the access issue without a bus.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, but the operating budget takes over after twelve months. Can we afford that?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, the previous groups were ""unaided."" If we set them up right, the cost is minimal.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm still worried about the roster, but A seems less demanding than running a whole mobile branch or a workshop.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I can support A. It's the least vulnerable to the external factors I'm worried about.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'll vote for A. It's the best compromise for the people who can't reach the main branch.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,"I'm hesitant about the grant, but B is a waste and C is a liability. A is the most reasonable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,A is the only one backed by a proven historical pattern in this system. I'm in.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If the partners do the heavy lifting, I can support A. It's the safest for the staff.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,It seems we are in agreement.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm happy we found a way to help the outer wards.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,George,,Let's hope the budget holds.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,May,,"It will, if we trust the community.","{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
